.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH trellis-release-pr 1 "" trellis "Trellis Manual"
.SH NAME
trellis\-release\-pr \- Create or update the release PR: version apply on a branch, push, open or refresh the PR via the GitHub API
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrellis release pr\fR [\fB\-\-bump\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-pre\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-resume\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-resume\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-pre\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-auto\-pre\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-unchanged\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-skip\-unchanged\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-prepare\-command\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-github\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create or update the release PR: version apply on a branch, push, open or refresh the PR via the GitHub API
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bump\fR \fI<LEVEL|PKG=LEVEL>\fR
Override the derived bump level, workspace\-wide (`\-\-bump major`) or for one package (`\-\-bump lat_core=major`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Run as if started in this directory
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to color output. `auto` follows the terminal, `NO_COLOR`, and `CLICOLOR=0`; the other two override that detection
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<PKG=VERSION>\fR
Pin a package\*(Aqs next version exactly (`\-\-set lat_core=1.0.0`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-pre\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
Cut or continue a prerelease cycle (`\-\-pre rc`). New cycles start at `<label>.0`; repeating the label increments the counter. Applying a candidate archives its new fragments. `\-\-pre none` selects promotion to the final version; applying it rolls up the archived candidates
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress normal\-path output; JSON/report payloads and errors still print
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<BASE>\fR [default: main]
Base branch the PR targets
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Trace every command trellis shells out to, on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR [default: release/pending]
Branch the release commit is force\-pushed to
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR
Don\*(Aqt check whether a newer trellis release is available

The check is also skipped in CI, when not attached to a terminal, and when `TRELLIS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` or `DO_NOT_TRACK` is set.
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR
Keep the pending PR\*(Aqs proposed package versions
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-resume\fR
Disable configured pending\-version resumption
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-pre\fR
Continue committed candidate labels when no mode was supplied or resumed
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-auto\-pre\fR
Disable configured automatic candidate continuation
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-unchanged\fR
Skip commit and push when release content and proposed versions have not changed
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-skip\-unchanged\fR
Disable configured content skipping (automatic mode still guards unchanged candidates)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Prepare even when content is unchanged; does not bypass validation
.TP
\fB\-\-prepare\-command\fR \fI<COMMAND>\fR
Run a shell command at the workspace root before committing; also validates unchanged releases
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the preparation outcome and package plan as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-github\-output\fR
Emit key=value records suitable for $GITHUB_OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
